# Line endings -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The runtime is Linux even when the repository is cloned on Windows: Compose
# files, Dockerfiles, the Makefile and Nginx configuration are consumed inside
# containers. With `core.autocrlf=true` (a common Windows default) a checkout
# rewrites them to CRLF, which breaks Dockerfile line continuations and shell
# snippets. Normalising to LF in the working tree keeps one checkout valid on
# both platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed inside the Linux containers. A CRLF checkout makes
# the kernel reject the shebang ("bad interpreter: /bin/sh^"), which on Windows
# only shows up at container start.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary

# Keep diffs readable.
frontend/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
